Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:19:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update libdatachannel: usrsctp restarts T3-rtx on a new
 cumulative ack

Pulls in a usrsctp fix for spurious retransmission timeouts: its express
SACK path never restarted the T3-rtx timer when the cumulative ack moved
(RFC 4960 6.3.2 R3), so with data in flight it expired every 2 x RTO and
cut cwnd to one MTU whenever the peer had delayed a SACK, as libwebrtc's
dcSCTP does for lone packets. This capped NetherNet (Minecraft Bedrock)
throughput at a few MTU per RTT (GeyserMC/Geyser#6854).

libdatachannel 548dfd075bfbd5c9df35552dfaafb408b711cbee

Written with assistance from Claude Code.
---
 .gitmodules        | 2 +-
 jni/libdatachannel | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.gitmodules b/.gitmodules
index fe4a864..032ad10 100644
--- a/.gitmodules
+++ b/.gitmodules
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 [submodule "jni/libdatachannel"]
 	path = jni/libdatachannel
-	url = https://github.com/opencollab-incubator/libdatachannel.git
+	url = https://github.com/onebeastchris/libdatachannel.git
 [submodule "jni/cmake-conan"]
 	path = jni/cmake-conan
 	url = https://github.com/conan-io/cmake-conan.git
diff --git a/jni/libdatachannel b/jni/libdatachannel
index 2e2d86a..548dfd0 160000
--- a/jni/libdatachannel
+++ b/jni/libdatachannel
@@ -1 +1 @@
-Subproject commit 2e2d86acc27a4734db2f28f95d09c1ab7a83836f
+Subproject commit 548dfd075bfbd5c9df35552dfaafb408b711cbee
